 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "centerCapacity[i] >= 1 is how many consecutive packages center i takes on each round-robin visit. Assignment starts at center 0. Each \"PACKAGE\" goes to the current center; once it has taken centerCapacity[i] packages in this visit, the turn passes to the next open center in increasing index order, wrapping around (possibly the same center when it is the only open one), and that visit starts from zero. \"CLOSURE i\" permanently closes open center i (never the last open center); if i is the current center the turn passes at once to the next open center, which starts a fresh visit. Return the index of the center that received the most packages in total (closed centers keep their totals); on a tie return the largest index.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk14-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
